Drop the explicit System.gc() on track change.

MusicController.play() called Utils.gc(false) immediately after reset() for
every new track. Utils.gc can invoke System.gc(), producing a stall at the
exact moment the player transitions to a new song. The generational
collector reclaims the short-lived objects from track teardown without a
forced full collection.

The itdelatrisu.opsu.Utils import becomes unused, which is a javac warning
rather than an error, so the import is left in place.

--- a/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/audio/MusicController.java
+++ b/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/audio/MusicController.java
@@ -101,7 +101,6 @@
 				return;
 			}
 
 			reset();
-			Utils.gc(false);
 
 			switch (BeatmapParser.getExtension(beatmap.audioFilename.getName())) {
